  "title": "Why does Ecuador have so many volcanoes? 🌋🇪🇨",
  "hook": "Why does Ecuador have so many volcanoes, and why are they all in a row?",
  "presenter": "perro",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "hook",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "and_hook",
      "narration": "Why does Ecuador have so many volcanoes, and why are they all in a row?",
      "on_screen_text": "Why so many volcanoes?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "volcanoes?"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "and_avenue",
      "narration": "There are dozens, and many of them form the famous Avenue of the Volcanoes, between two mountain ranges.",
      "on_screen_text": "The Avenue of the Volcanoes",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Avenue"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sub_plates",
      "narration": "Blame two plates: the Nazca Plate, under the ocean, and the South American Plate, where the continent sits.",
      "on_screen_text": "Two plates collide",
      "highlight_words": [
        "collide"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sub_push",
      "narration": "The Nazca Plate pushes east and slides underneath the continent.",
      "on_screen_text": "Nazca slides underneath",
      "highlight_words": [
        "underneath"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sub_melt",
      "narration": "About a hundred kilometers down, it releases the water it had trapped, and that water makes the mantle melt.",
      "on_screen_text": "Water melts the mantle",
      "highlight_words": [
        "melts"
      ],
      "sfx": "bubbles",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sub_rise",
      "narration": "That magma rises, punches through the crust and builds a volcano right above.",
      "on_screen_text": "The magma rises",
      "highlight_words": [
        "rises"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sub_row",
      "narration": "Since the collision happens along the whole coast, the volcanoes line up, from north to south.",
      "on_screen_text": "That's why they line up",
      "highlight_words": [
        "line"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "and_rise",
      "narration": "And that same push slowly lifted the Andes over millions of years.",
      "on_screen_text": "How the Andes grew",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Andes"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "and_cotopaxi",
      "narration": "Cotopaxi, almost six thousand meters tall, is one of the highest active volcanoes in the world.",
      "on_screen_text": "Cotopaxi: almost 6,000 m",
      "highlight_words": [
        "6,000"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "role": "surprise",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "and_globe",
      "narration": "And the summit of Chimborazo is the farthest point from the center of the Earth, even farther than Everest.",
      "on_screen_text": "Farther than Everest",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Everest"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "gal_map",
      "narration": "And guess which plate carries the Galápagos toward Ecuador? The same one: the Nazca Plate.",
      "on_screen_text": "The same plate!",
      "highlight_words": [
        "same"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "and_final",
      "narration": "So every volcano in Ecuador is a sign that the ocean floor is sliding under your feet.",
      "on_screen_text": "The ocean, under your feet",
      "highlight_words": [
        "feet"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
