  "description": "Ecuador has dozens of volcanoes lined up north to south because the Nazca Plate sinks beneath the South American Plate (subduction). About 100 km down, the plate releases water, the mantle melts and magma rises to build volcanoes like Cotopaxi. Chimborazo's summit is the point on Earth's surface farthest from its center. Original 3D animation; not to scale, figures are approximate.",
